# AI Networking Workshop: From LLMs to Production Agents
## Complete Workshop Outline & Agenda (macOS Compatible)

**Version:** 2.0 (macOS/Mock Devices)  
**Date:** March 31, 2026  
**Duration:** 3.25 hours (195 minutes)  
**Format:** Hands-on workshop with live instruction  
**Target Audience:** Network engineers ready to build AI agents  

---

## Executive Summary

This hands-on workshop teaches network professionals how to build production-ready AI agents for network operations. Unlike traditional workshops that focus on *using* AI tools, this session teaches you to *build* AI systems from scratch.

**Key Innovation:** All labs run natively on macOS using realistic mock network devices, removing infrastructure barriers while teaching production-ready AI agent development.

### What Makes This Different

**Most AI Workshops:**
- Show you how to use ChatGPT/Copilot
- Focus on prompting existing tools
- Limited customization

**This Workshop:**
- Build AI agents from scratch
- Understand LLM internals
- Create autonomous network agents
- Deploy to real infrastructure (path provided)

### Technology Stack

**Primary Tools:**
- **Ollama** - Local LLMs (free)
- **Python 3.10+** - Agent development
- **Ollama** - 100% free local LLM (llama3.2:3b)
- **Mock Network Devices** - macOS-compatible simulator

**Optional (Demo Only):**
- Containerlab + Arista cEOS (instructor demos)

**Cost to Participants:** $0-10 (Ollama free, $10 optional API credits)

---

